invariant: INV-11
file: srv_flight.c
catches: srv_flight_test_aes
reason: the server names TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 in its ServerHello and
  keys both handshake directions with ChaCha20, which is what 9aa1f65
  shipped: srv_select chose the suite and no keying site read it. Every
  test that stops at the selection passes, and a client that took the
  suite from the ServerHello fails to open the EncryptedExtensions.
  test_flight_key_suite opens the server's first sealed record under an
  AES-GCM reader keyed on its own.

--- old
    REC_DIR_INIT_SUITE(&t->rd, h->c_hs, sel->suite);
    REC_DIR_INIT_SUITE(&t->wr, h->s_hs, sel->suite);
--- new
    rec_dir_init(&t->rd, h->c_hs);
    rec_dir_init(&t->wr, h->s_hs);
